    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch02-10: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.62";
    dc:description "Current divergence can proxy species formation in well-sampled clades, but no global dataset consistently identifies incipient species. Available data test restricted groups and depend on contested speciation metrics.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Estimate current incipient-speciation rates from genomic divergence, reproductive isolation and lineage splitting, then test whether they increase with existing genus richness after age and sampling controls. A positive average relationship supports the prediction.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "'Still forming' is not directly observable.", "Genus age and taxonomic practice strongly confound richness.";
